---
description: Local document OCR, extraction and legal identity safety
globs: sro_robot/core/*.py,sro_robot/documents/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Keep document processing local; do not send files or OCR text to cloud AI.
- Do not reduce the multi-pass OCR approach without measured regression evidence.
- Treat checksums and heuristics as evidence, not proof of participant identity.
- Bind FIO, tax identifiers, address and birth data to the same legally relevant participant/role. An applicant is not necessarily the debtor.
- Preserve field source/provenance and warnings. Never invent unreadable values.
- Document date selection must avoid hearing dates in later text. Case-number normalization must handle known OCR Latin/Cyrillic confusion.
- Ambiguous document type, act selection, participant role or operation must stop for human review.
- Use synthetic fixtures. Sample files may be absent or user-managed; never assume old samples still exist or restore them without instruction.
